    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d518">

                <pb facs="0768" n="652" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg652"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1123 Lincheng/123: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-06-02T18:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 2, 1923—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received June 2—8:45 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of May 31, noon [<hi rendition="#italic">4 p.m.?</hi>].
                    Davis telegraphs 2 o’clock this afternoon: Henley,<anchor n="91"
                        xml:id="d518-f1"/> Eddy Elias,<anchor n="92" xml:id="d518-f2"/>
                        Saphiere<anchor n="92" xml:id="d518-f3"/> and Verea<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d518-f4"/> unconditionally released.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cunningham</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d518-f1" n="91" xml:id="d518-f1-content">
                <p>J. A. Henley, American citizen.</p>
